      <guid>https://larecs.github.io/larecs/pr-preview/pr-243/larecs/resource_representation/PlainValue/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;Mojo trait&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/larecs/larecs/blob/003dea471daba8a096b7cd84bd507481ea9a39fe/src/larecs/resource_representation.mojo#L10&#34;&gt;Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;plainvalue&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;PlainValue&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Declares that a trivial type stores only plain numeric values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conform when reflection cannot inspect a pointer-free representation,
such as a &lt;code&gt;StaticTuple&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;InlineArray&lt;/code&gt; field of scalars. The declaring
author guarantees that no field, at any depth, holds a pointer, reference,
or handle; Larecs cannot verify this. Declared types must still be
trivially copyable, movable, and deletable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Implemented traits&lt;span class=&#34;hx-absolute -hx-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;implemented-traits&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
